From 0e85c5254cb015a544c3cd8e6d8f8afd0aa086d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "suricata.lu" <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:21:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: ti: cpsw-proxy-client: drop skip_fdq from
 k3_udma_glue_reset_rx_chn()

CIP patch 0574 (upstream 0da30874729b "dmaengine: ti: k3-udma-glue:
Drop skip_fdq argument from k3_udma_glue_reset_rx_chn") removed the
skip_fdq argument and converted the upstream callers. TI's CPSW Proxy
Client is not upstream, so it still passed the old fifth argument and
no longer builds.

It resets flow 0 with skip_fdq = false. The function now skips the
free descriptor queue only when the channel uses a single FDQ and
flow_num is not 0, so dropping the argument keeps the behaviour.
ti-linux-6.18.y makes the same call with four arguments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/ti/cpsw-proxy-client.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/cpsw-proxy-client.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/cpsw-proxy-client.c
index 83218e3a7faa9..11be005e8de28 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/cpsw-proxy-client.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/cpsw-proxy-client.c
@@ -1710,8 +1710,7 @@ static void vport_stop(struct virtual_port *vport)
 		k3_udma_glue_rx_flow_disable(rx_chn->rx_chan, 0);
 		/* Need some delay to process RX ring before reset */
 		msleep(100);
-		k3_udma_glue_reset_rx_chn(rx_chn->rx_chan, 0, rx_chn, vport_rx_cleanup,
-					  false);
+		k3_udma_glue_reset_rx_chn(rx_chn->rx_chan, 0, rx_chn, vport_rx_cleanup);
 		napi_disable(&rx_chn->napi_rx);
 		hrtimer_cancel(&rx_chn->rx_hrtimer);
 	}
